<%# Join/Leave membership toggle button.
    Single implementation shared by the club card and the club show page, so
    styling, progress text and the leave confirmation can never drift between
    the initial render and turbo-stream updates.
    Rails' button_to puts id/class/data on the inner <button> (only +form+
    opts land on the <form>), so the leave confirmation is set on BOTH the
    button (submitter, which Turbo checks first) and the form (fallback) — it
    must not silently disappear after a turbo-stream swap.
    Locals:
    - club: BookClub (required)
    - is_member: Boolean (required)
    - join_label / leave_label: String (required)
    - joining_label / leaving_label: String - progress text (required)
    - join_button_class / leave_button_class: String - full button classes (required)
    - button_id: String (optional - show page sets it for turbo targeting/tests)
    - form_class: String (optional extra class for the generated form) %>
  <% button_id ||= nil %>
  <% form_class ||= nil %>
  <% confirm_message = is_member ? t("leave_club_confirm") : nil %>
  <%= button_to is_member ? leave_label : join_label,
  book_club_membership_path(club),
  method: :post,
  id: button_id,
  form: {
    class: form_class,
    data: {
      turbo_frame: "_top",
      turbo_confirm: confirm_message,
    },
  },
  data: {
    turbo_submits_with: is_member ? leaving_label : joining_label,
    turbo_confirm: confirm_message,
  },
  class: is_member ? leave_button_class : join_button_class %>
